      <h1>Abhishek Karna</h1>
      <p class="role">PhD student in physics, Princeton University</p>

      <!-- Introduction: replace with your own text. -->
      <p>
        I work on machine learning for quantum materials with
        <a href="https://bernevig-group.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">B. Andrei Bernevig</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before Princeton I studied physics and mathematics at Duke University, with a certificate in
        philosophy, politics and economics. At Duke I developed a
        <a href="https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/gtbl-vsdt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">quantum Monte Carlo method for lattice Hamiltonians</a>
        with <a href="https://scholars.duke.edu/person/sch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shailesh Chandrasekharan</a>,
        and synthesized and grew crystals of quantum magnets in
        <a href="https://scholars.duke.edu/person/Sara.Haravifard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sara Haravifard</a>'s lab.
      </p>

